reference_use.conclusion:
The two ingredients of the selected theorem are not stated anywhere locally: the Gram-determinant/compression identity and the measurability of sqrt det(p L* L p + I − p). I searched the local snapshot, the project GMT tree, SimonGMT and the 509-node DAG. The closest DAG items, dgoj_det_adjoint_comp_eq_det_sq and fvmb_gram_det_le_exp_sum_norm_sq_sub, are different statements. Both children are therefore new, and the proposed names have no hits anywhere.

The pinned Mathlib (25730c7c) supplies everything the child proofs need:
- ContinuousLinearMap.det, an abbrev for LinearMap.det, and ContinuousLinearMap.continuous_det;
- LinearMap.det_eq_det_mul_det: the determinant is the determinant of the restriction to an invariant submodule times that of the induced quotient map (proved via Matrix.det_fromBlocks_zero₂₁);
- LinearMap.det_toMatrix;
- the Submodule.starProjection API: starProjection_apply_mem, starProjection_eq_self_iff, starProjection_apply_eq_zero_iff, inner_starProjection_left_eq_right, isCompl_orthogonal;
- ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right;
- OrthonormalBasis.repr_apply_apply and coe_toBasis_repr_apply.

Lean checks in the frozen contract scope:
- All three types elaborate.
- Both children were fully proved; the scripts are embedded in their natural proofs and compile with no errors or warnings, using only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.
- The exact frozen parent type was proved from them by simp_rw with child 1 (V := Q x, e := stdOrthonormalBasis) followed by exact child 2 (p := fun x => (Q x).starProjection).

An independent reviewer re-ran the checks and confirmed byte-identical types, instance agreement and name uniqueness. Simon Ch. 3 formula 2.3 (book/chapter-03.txt line 365) is the source identity J^M_f = sqrt(det Gram) = sqrt(det(d^M f* d^M f)); the measurability remark is at line 385.

